AUDIO: 'access to that. But it\'s been so so good. And I feel like whenever I start feeling off on social media, I\'m seeing things that are making me feel worse after I\'ve been scrolling, that\'s when I know it\'s time to lock everything up,'

[04:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and that\'s my cue to go tap my NFC tag. Who knew a piece of marble would be so effective at helping me quit social media? For all of these other NFC use cases, I\'m going to be using the Shortcuts app to program my NFC tag'

[04:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because the Shortcut app makes it super easy to do that. What\'s really handy within the Shortcuts app is your ability to set up automation. So essentially when you scan your NFC tag, you can set up a sequence of events that happen'

[04:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'simultaneously. Instead of you having to do these individual steps, your phone kind of takes care of all of that for you. Some of my favorite NFC tags actually are ones that initiate certain modes in my life. So one of them being'

[05:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as we\'re sitting here in the office, my work mode. I\'ve had an NFC sticker stuck to the inside of one of my top office drawers for a few years now. And whenever I tap my phone against it, it goes through this sequence of events. It'

[05:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'vibrates my device, which I really like a vibration at the beginning because then I can know that the automation has run without me looking at my screen to confirm. Then it turns on my work focus till 5:00 p.m. Now, if you\'ve never heard of focuses before, these are'

[05:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'essentially custom home screens and notification settings that you can set up for different points of your day. So, I have a work mode focus, which essentially turns off any social'

[05:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'notifications and only allows work notifications like emails through my home screen. Also has all of my work apps on it. Got fun little background wallpaper moment happening there just to set the tone. It also then starts a 30'

[05:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'minute timer. So again, like I can have a focus 30 minute work session. And usually after 30 minutes, I like to take a 5minut break. It\'s kind of like a pomodoro method style that I like to do. I don\'t like to do like hour, two hour'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'long sessions without getting up from my desk cuz then I just feel like it really fatigues you after a bit. And I have it open up the YouTube app so I can quickly put on some working background music cuz I usually like to have some sort of instrumentals when I\'m working. And that'

[06:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'essentially is my work mode. And all of these things happen in a matter of seconds when I scan the app. It would take me, you know, maybe a minute or two to do it manually myself. So, yes, I\'m only saving seconds, but there\'s'

[06:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something that really pushes me to use this when I know like it is so easy to get everything going. To know I can scan this and focus immediately on getting in the zone, really helps. One of my other favorite focuses is a reading mode'

[06:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'focus. So, whenever I want to have a reading session, whether it\'s for a fiction or a non-fiction book, I turn this on on my phone typically, and it pulls together all of my favorite reading apps like Libby and Fable. I\'m now just on Fable, actually. If you want'

